    {
      "id": 29,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -1026.1966781263839,
        -34.54667131403989
      ],
      "size": [
        646.8917489487137,
        417.03948542060874
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 12,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "ue_properties": {
          "widget_ue_connectable": {},
          "version": "7.5.2",
          "input_ue_unconnectable": {}
        }
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "MARKDKBERRY.com\n\nThis originated in Krita ACLY plugin, where I had the best results and less failures, but it took too long. So I exported it here, and have adapted it for my needs. - Feb 2026.\n\n- I presume you will find your own models and loras but search civitai or hugging face with the names, if you want the ones shown in the slots in this wf.\n\n---\n\n- Check this reddit post out about using Lighting 8 steps lora for improvements (I think it improves on the 4 step) and also discussion about the plastic skin issues and lora fixes for it: \n\n[https://www.reddit.com/r/comfyui/comments/1q5z3b8/lightx2v_just_released_their_8step_lightning_lora/](https://www.reddit.com/r/comfyui/comments/1q5z3b8/lightx2v_just_released_their_8step_lightning_lora)\n\n---\n\n## LORAS:\n\n- For blending a cut and paste person/object better, try the fusion lora from here\n https://huggingface.co/dx8152/Qwen-Image-Edit-2509-Fusion\n\t- The trigger words are: 溶图,纠正产品透视角度和光影并使产品融入背景   \n\t(translation: *Blend the image, correct the product's perspective and lighting, and integrate the product into the background.*).\n\n\n- For better skin apparently this lora - https://huggingface.co/valiantcat/Qwen-Image-Edit-2509-photous/tree/main\n</br>\n- BSF head and face swap - https://huggingface.co/Alissonerdx/BFS-Best-Face-Swap\n```\nhead_swap: start with Picture 1 as the base image, keeping its lighting, environment, and background. remove the head from Picture 1 completely and replace it with the head from Picture 2, strictly preserving the hair, eye color, and nose structure of Picture 2. copy the eye direction, head rotation, and micro-expressions from Picture 1. high quality, sharp details, 4k\n````\n\n\n\n## ISSUES:\n\n- weak point for this workflow currently is character consistency when using 2nd image reference to push character into image 1. needs more testing and comparing to ones that do it better. - Feb 2026.\n\n\n\n"
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
